[{"text":"GAE[mu] can be used as input for a D-4-dimensional \\(\\gamma^{\\mu }\\)and is transformed into DiracGamma[LorentzIndex[mu, D-4], D-4] by FeynCalcInternal (FCI).","anchor":"gae"},{"text":"GAE[mu, nu , ...] is a short form for GAE[mu].GAE[nu] ....","anchor":"gae"},{"text":"Overview, DiracGamma, GA, GS, GAD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"GAE[\\[Mu]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GAE[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]] - GAE[\\[Nu], \\[Mu]]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\nu }-\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\nu }.\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"StandardForm[FCI[GAE[\\[Mu]]]] (*DiracGamma[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu], -4 + D], -4 + D]*)","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GAE[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Sigma]]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\nu }.\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\rho }.\\hat{\\gamma }^{\\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"StandardForm[GAE[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Sigma]]] (*GAE[\\[Mu]] . GAE[\\[Nu]] . GAE[\\[Rho]] . GAE[\\[Sigma]]*)","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GAE[\\[Alpha]] FVD[p, \\[Alpha]] // Contract","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{p}\\]","anchor":"cb6-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GAE[\\[Alpha]] FV[p, \\[Alpha]] // Contract","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"In order to use Dirac algebra with D-4-dimensional objects you need to activate the t’Hooft-Veltman-Breitenlohner-Maison scheme first","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"] DiracSimplify[GAE[\\[Mu]] . GAD[\\[Mu]]]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{NDR}\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{\\$Aborted}